        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Budget roughly $300 to $650 for a basic DIY two-car floor, $800 to $1,800 for a thicker DIY system done properly, and $1,800 to $4,500 for a professional flake floor, then adjust for your slab and region. The kit price is never the full story: grinder rental, repairs, topcoats and your own time all belong in the total.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Measured per year of service, the options sit closer together than their sticker prices suggest. Pick the one that matches your slab, your schedule and how long you plan to stay, spend on preparation before anything decorative, and get every professional quote in writing with the system spelled out layer by layer.
          </p>
        </div>

